# fixedbugs, M-robustness-guards step 3, 2026-09-03 (panel 103's
# ffi-pragmatist, measured on three clangs).
#
# SYMPTOM: `@n: i64` against `size_t *` — the right width, the wrong sign —
# built at exit 0 on every clang. `-Werror=incompatible-pointer-types` does not
# see it: `long *` against `unsigned long *` is `-Wpointer-sign`, a warning
# nobody escalates, on clang 18, 21 and 22 alike. So the strict flag alone
# could never have been the check, and the compiler's own check asks about
# sign as well as width.
#
# CAUSE and FIX: as `ffi-pointee-width.hero`'s, one file over — the same two
# `_Static_assert`s, and this is the one the second half of the pair catches:
# `((time_t)-1 > 0) == ((uint64_t)-1 > 0)` is false. `time(time_t *)` is the
# witness because `time_t` is a signed 64-bit integer on all three platforms
# (`long` on the Mac and Linux, `__int64` on Windows), so `@t: u64` is the sign
# mistake on every leg, where `getline`'s `size_t *` exists on only two.
extern "time.h"
    function time(@t: u64) -> i64  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    t: u64 @ 0
    _ = time(@t)
    print(t > 0)
